* Behringer UMC22 U-Phoria
	* this is a cheap but quality "audio interface"
	* it contains both an input and an output DAC+amp
	* thus it can function as a headphone amplifier too, as such it is neutral sounding but somewhat metalic, but it still is not difficult to listen to for long time
* FiiO E10K Olympus 2
	* cheap, small headphone amplifier
	* sound
		* clean, smooth, thick
		* no harshness, no sibilance, no metalic timbre
			* easy to listen to for long time
		* as if it was elevated at around 160 Herz
		* stage is small
		* compared to K11
			* the K11 in filter mode 1 is better in almost every aspect, but especially in detail and separation of instruments
			* still the difference in overall sound quality is not huge, if you have the E10K than you can remain satisfied with it, no need to update to a K11
* Beyerdynamic A 20
	* neutral, non-offensive, never harsh, maybe a little more tightness would be better
	* could drive my Sennheiser Game One with acceptable sound quality; this is notable because that headphone usually sounds unpleasantly wet
* Topping L30
	* is warm all the time, even on smallest gain, even when no sound is played
	* sound
		* lean
		* thin, but still wet
		* my Sennheiser 6xx sounded awesome on it
		* my Superlux 672 did not show a big quality improvement by switching from cheap Behringer UMC22 to this amp
* Sabaj A10h
	* similar to Topping L30, but somewhat more blant and less neutral, feels less correct
* Topping DX3 Pro+
	* sound differs from the L30
	* clean, sweet, warm, too blunt, a little overemphasis somewhere in the mids or high-lows [especially for piano]
	* pushes the music in my face too much, hence spatial properties are bad
	* the FiiO E10K is similar sound for 4 times less money
* FiiO K11
	* looks elegant on the desk - a little friendly box
	* sound in single-ended mode
		* detailed, even too much, as it sounds to be trying to be detailed
		* instrument-separation is much
		* stage is big enough
		* the DAC filters
			* are audibly different
			* contain a no-oversampling mode
		* i liked the sound of the FiiO E10K more
			* the E10K is more musical to me, more coherent, the K11 sounds too "digital" to me
* FiiO K7
	* sound in single ended mode
		* dry
		* nicely disappears in the mids
		* bass missing?
	* the light is big and hurts my eye